WEBVTT

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:20.060
The sex, the pep, the pep, the pie, and the home sweet home.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:34.590
I'll strike oil in a minute, and I haven't seen an angle worm yet.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.250
No wonder. You're digging straight down.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.770
You gotta dig on angles for angle worms.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.520
Gee, I'm glad we shook Pinhead.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:46.950
Yeah, if he knew we were going fishing, we'd never get rid of him.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.220
Digging anymore. There's no worms here.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:58.870
Ah, shucks.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:00:59.970
What did you do with...

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.390
apple with a worm in it.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:10.320
Was you afraid it wasn't coming?

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.410
No, we were afraid it was.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.530
You haven't even got any worms.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.610
Go on, scram.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.820
or

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.970
Remember when we're sick, Joe.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.920
Yeah, then you sat on my bed and ate it.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:44.120
Say, boss, hadn't we better send that heap to the junkyard?

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.500
Nothing doing! Don't you remember what Barnum said?

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.050
Gee, is that a nifty-looking car?

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.110
Yeah, it's elegant!

00:02:58.730 --> 00:02:59.290
Fine!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.210
Sure, I got a quarter, and I got 20 cents.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.110
All we need is another nickel.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.460
Pinhead's got a nickel.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.980
Come on, fork over.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.490
Nothing doing, I ain't gonna blow it on automobiles.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.380
Boys, there's a bargain that can't last long.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.610
That's what I'm afraid of.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.760
It's apt to go up anytime.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.460
Hop in for a demonstration.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:37.960
This car belonged to an aristocrat.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.040
Family came over in the Mayflower.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.530
Did they bring this car with them?

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:49.430
This car's got some real power behind it.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.300
I bet it would go a mile a minute.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.770
Oh, much better than that.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.690
I'd be afraid to open it up.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.140
Yeah, the moss might fly out.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:29.970
Well, boys, she's yours for fifty...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.400
Cents down oh

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:50.200
Here's his and here's mine there. Thanks boys

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:02.200
Thank you.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.730
Give me one gallon.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:36.700
What? Just one gallon for that car?

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.450
Yeah, we're weaning it.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.390
Hey, these tires are flat.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.500
They're only flat on one side.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.000
Get the air hose.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.560
You've done enough already.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:40.410
Well, we sure picked a light car.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.440
It's liable to light any place.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:01.980
it

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.720
Well, we'll take advance.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.700
It's been snuffing their telephone pole.

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:02.790
Maybe he's...

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.100
Quick, give me that pole.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:37.650
My dad, how do you know that the fish broad is on scale?
